Track 1: Molten Lead Sweeps the Third Rail
- Story & Context: On the midnight departure out of Ibadan, sound engineer Kofi St. Cloud recorded a local street-band jamming alongside a broken train engine using a pocket synth plugged into a portable reel-to-reel tape deck. The engine sparked, casting blue glare across the glass windows as the synth brass hummed its first legendary polyrhythmic hook. Over the roaring track, a soprano singer belted out "Light the furnace inside the glass house before the dawn arrives" to wake the sleeping passengers. The resulting bootleg cassette was duplicated three hundred times and sold out of coat pockets across rail stations from Accra to London, founding the genre overnight.
