Track 2: Koforidua Glassworks
- Story & Context: Written during a three-day snowstorm delay inside a stationary rail carriage in northern France, synthesizer technician Amara Vance sat in the dark watching her breath freeze against the double-paned glass. Armed with a pocket synth and a glass bottle, she tapped out a delicate, crystalline Highlife rhythm against the frosty window frame while singing "I am holding the cracked vase until my fingers bleed gold" into a low-fidelity condenser mic. The sound captured her isolation, blending the coldness of European winter with the warm, resilient lilt of her Ghanaian childhood. The band added mellotron flutes during post-production, transforming a lonely moment into a soaring, symphonic character portrait.
